# Line endings are part of this repository's contract, not a local preference.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true by default, which rewrites
# every checked-out text file to CRLF. That is invisible on macOS/Linux CI and
# breaks real things here:
#
#   * The CLI round-trips ServiceNow record fields through local files and
#     compares them byte-for-byte to decide what changed (`build --diff`, the
#     mirror's serializer and its manifest hashes). A CRLF checkout makes a
#     clean tree read as fully-modified.
#   * Test fixtures and expected-output files are compared as bytes, so a CRLF
#     checkout reddens suites that pass everywhere else.
#   * `packaging/windows/install.ps1` and `packages/mcp-server/scripts/
#     quality-gates.sh` are executed, not just read; a shell script that reaches
#     WSL/Linux with CRLF fails on the shebang line.
#
# `.editorconfig` already declares `end_of_line = lf` for the whole tree, but it
# only governs editors — it cannot influence what git writes at checkout time.
# This file makes the same rule hold at the git layer, for every contributor,
# regardless of their core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Every tracked text file is already LF in the index (verified with
# `git ls-files --eol`), so this normalises nothing retroactively; it only keeps
# the working tree matching the index on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary content: never normalise it, never try to diff it as text.
*.png binary
